---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import siteData from '../data/site.json';

const breadcrumbItems = [
  { name: 'About Atrium Livings' }
];

const authors = siteData.authors;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Atrium Livings | Architectural Standards & Masthead"
  description="Learn about Atrium Livings's editorial standards, licensed architectural advisory board, historic preservation ethics, and commitment to original residential reporting."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbItems}
  jsonLdType="organization"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbItems} />

  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="container about-container">
      <span class="about-kicker">Our Manifesto</span>
      <h1 class="about-headline">Architecture as an Enduring Art Form</h1>
      <p class="about-lead">
        Atrium Livings was founded on a singular conviction: residential interior design is not an accumulation of fleeting seasonal trends, but the disciplined orchestration of light, acoustics, materiality, and human volume.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-body-section">
    <div class="container about-container">
      <div class="about-prose">
        <h2>The Editorial Mission & Spatial Philosophy</h2>
        <p>
          In an online publishing landscape increasingly compromised by superficial trends, automated affiliate clickbait, and ephemeral lifestyle fads, Atrium Livings provides an uncompromised sanctuary for discerning architects, structural designers, and passionate homeowners. We treat residential design not as casual decoration, but as an applied physical discipline—an intricate orchestration of spatial geometry, dynamic solar pathing, acoustic insulation, and tactile materiality.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every dwelling tells a story of human volume and structural economy. When an interior environment is conceived with rigorous precision, everyday rituals transcend utility: waking up to calibrated morning daylight entering through high clerestory windows, feeling the unbroken tactile relief of honed French limestone under bare feet, and enjoying the stillness achieved through staggered-stud acoustic wall damping. Our editorial commitment is to dismantle the barrier between professional architectural theory and accessible residential execution.
        </p>

        <div class="editorial-highlight-box">
          <h3>Our Three Foundational Pillars</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Material Honesty & Patina:</strong> We champion authentic natural stone, unlacquered living brass, lime-based mineral plasters, and certified solid hardwoods that develop rich depth through human interaction rather than synthetic chemical veneers engineered for premature obsolescence.</li>
            <li><strong>Technical Rigor & Tolerances:</strong> We mandate concrete clearance tolerances, tile grout matrix chemistry, subfloor deflection ratios (L/360 and L/720), HVAC acoustic decibel thresholds, and regional seismic codes—empowering homeowners to engage general contractors and structural engineers as informed peers.</li>
            <li><strong>Uncompromising Editorial Independence:</strong> No product placement or brand endorsement is ever accepted for compensation. We never sell editorial recommendations. Every specification, fixture review, and material evaluation reflects rigorous physical studio testing and peer-reviewed architectural merit.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2>Architectural Critique & Rigorous Testing Methodology</h2>
        <p>
          Unlike conventional shelter magazines that rely solely on glossy PR photographs, Atrium Livings subjects design trends, building products, and architectural details to structured engineering and material evaluations. Before any countertop stone, timber species, or glazing assembly is featured in our guides, it is examined across four key metrics:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Structural Durability & Lifecycle Footprint:</strong> We calculate lifecycle cost per annum, analyzing whether high-initial-cost materials—such as sintered stone slabs or reclaimed quarter-sawn white oak—deliver superior financial and environmental returns across a 30-year residential timeline compared to mass-market laminates.</li>
          <li><strong>Thermal Dynamics & Daylighting Optimization:</strong> We evaluate how window fenestration, low-E coatings, solar heat gain coefficients (SHGC), and thermal mass walls influence interior microclimates, significantly lowering active HVAC electrical loads through passive architectural design.</li>
          <li><strong>Acoustic Isolation & Decibel Attenuation:</strong> In an era of high-ceiling open-concept floor plans, acoustic reverberation frequently impairs psychological comfort. We calculate Noise Reduction Coefficients (NRC) and Sound Transmission Class (STC) ratings for acoustic wall panels, acoustic plaster, and underlayments.</li>
          <li><strong>Indoor Air Quality (IAQ) & Biophilic Chemistry:</strong> We promote living spaces free from toxic volatile organic compounds (VOCs). We rigorously test natural lime washes, milk paints, zero-VOC natural plant oils, and formaldehyde-free structural plywood to ensure residences nurture physical wellness.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Bridging the Architect-Contractor Divide</h2>
        <p>
          A chronic pain point in residential renovation is the persistent disconnect between architectural vision and job-site trade execution. High design frequently founders on poor site communication, misplaced rough-in plumbing coordinates, or miscalculated subfloor heights. Atrium Livings actively resolves this friction by publishing trade-tested specification cards and millimeter-precise architectural drawings.
        </p>
        <p>
          We provide our readership with the exact questions to ask subcontractors during pre-construction meetings: verifying whether a curbless walk-in shower pan has been properly recessed into the joist plane, whether waterproofing conforms to ANSI A118.10 standards, and whether custom floor-to-ceiling pivot doors incorporate concealed hydraulic closers with independent speed valves. By bridging high design intent with tactical site craft, we turn ambitious blueprints into enduring sanctuaries.
        </p>

        <h2>The Editorial Masthead</h2>
        <p>
          Our senior editors and regular contributors are licensed architects (AIA), structural designers, LEED-accredited environmental consultants, and architectural historians with advanced credentials from the world's preeminent design institutions, including Harvard GSD, Columbia GSAPP, and Sorbonne Paris IV.
        </p>

        <div class="masthead-grid">
          {authors.map(author => (
            <div class="masthead-card">
              <img src={author.avatar} alt={author.name} width="90" height="90" class="masthead-img" />
              <div class="masthead-content">
                <h3 class="masthead-name"><a href={`/author/${author.slug}`}>{author.name}</a></h3>
                <span class="masthead-role">{author.role}</span>
                <span class="masthead-creds">{author.credentials}</span>
                <p class="masthead-bio">{author.bio}</p>
                <a href={`/author/${author.slug}`} class="masthead-link">View Published Portfolio &rarr;</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <h2>Physical Publishing Headquarters</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Atrium Livings Media Group, Inc.</strong><br />
          742 Montgomery Street, Suite 400<br />
          Jackson Square Historic District<br />
          San Francisco, CA 94111 &bull; United States<br />
          ISSN: 2984-1184 (Global Architecture Edition)
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    background-color: var(--color-surface-subtle);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 4.5rem 0 3.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .about-container {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .about-kicker {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .about-headline {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .about-lead {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .about-body-section {
    padding: 4rem 0 6rem;
  }

  .about-prose {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #2D2A26;
  }

  .about-prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.85rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .editorial-highlight-box {
    background-color: var(--color-surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding: 2rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  .editorial-highlight-box h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .editorial-highlight-box ul {
    list-style: square;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .masthead-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 3.5rem;
  }

  .masthead-card {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.75rem;
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .masthead-img {
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .masthead-name {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }

  .masthead-role {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .masthead-creds {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text-light);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .masthead-bio {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .masthead-link {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-dark);
  }

  .masthead-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .masthead-card {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>